{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: add honest resident-rebuild progress to the browser when a fold-profile version bump invalidates the prior checkpoint.\n\nObserved on 2026-08-10 after workroom-fold@2 reached main and the resident was rebuilt at depth about 2,868. The HTML and hashed UI assets returned immediately, while /v0/status and /v0/actors returned zero bytes for minutes under Workspace.Snapshot's cold audit. The browser showed only “Loading work…”, which looked like a broken bundle. Presence, worktrees, and graph remained responsive. The verifier eventually wrote a valid @2 checkpoint; /v0/status then returned the 5.5 MB projection in about 20 ms and the UI recovered.\n\nThis is a usability child of the existing head-notice/single-flight request, not an urgent production blocker for the current single-user preview. Preserve the audit: do not fake readiness, skip verification, or label an old projection current.","body":{"conditions":"During a cold verified rebuild, especially after a fold-profile/checkpoint version bump, the resident exposes a bounded progress view that is readable without waiting on the full snapshot mutex; the browser replaces generic “Loading work…” with an accessible phase and measured progress such as verified N of total, explains that durable history is being verified, and does not imply failure or currentness; if a previously verified projection exists it may remain readable only with an explicit rebuilding/stale-frontier qualifier, while first startup may show progress without work data; canceled or duplicate HTTP readers do not start duplicate cold audits; normal warm startup remains quiet; tests force a profile mismatch over scaled history and prove progress advances, the final exact projection replaces it, and no unverified projection is served.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}